From f780a9fc7756cb5ffc677321cf876f8e344974f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:51:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] add a LICENSE file

Upstream-Status: To upstream [no LICENSE file exists anywhere in the adrian-lorenz/leakguard repository, despite pyproject.toml declaring `license = { text = "MIT" }` and every classifier/README badge claiming MIT; this carries the standard MIT boilerplate matching that declared intent until upstream publishes the text itself]

pyproject.toml's [project] table carries no license-files key, so maturin
falls back to its default LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING*/NOTICE*/AUTHORS* glob next
to pyproject.toml (same rule as setuptools' PEP 639 default) -- but there
is nothing there to glob: the checkout, every tagged release, and every
wheel published on PyPI (confirmed against 1.0.4's real
manylinux_2_17_x86_64 wheel) ship a "License: MIT" metadata string and
zero bytes of actual licence text in dist-info. RISE distributes this
wheel, so the gap is ours to close.

Add the standard MIT licence text, attributing the copyright to Adrian
Lorenz (the sole committer, per `git log --format='%an <%ae>'`) for 2026
(the year of every commit in the history). No pyproject.toml or
Cargo.toml edit is needed: dropping the file at the project root is
enough for maturin's existing default glob to pick it up into
dist-info/licenses/LICENSE, confirmed with a local
`maturin build --release` before and after the patch.
---
 LICENSE | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE

diff --git a/LICENSE b/LICENSE
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e97f5d3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+MIT License
+
+Copyright (c) 2026 Adrian Lorenz
+
+Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
